From f63aea6b7f47ec584588548f0d946c6ce5a0b472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 06:10:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add SSH-key login option for Node installer and Cloud VPS
 creation

Both flows now let the user choose between password and SSH-key auth
instead of only ever using a password:

- Node installer: after the SSH username, ask password vs. private key.
  ssh_client.py's RemoteSession now supports asyncssh key-based auth
  alongside password auth, including sudo detection when no password is
  available to pipe into `sudo -S` (raises a clear error telling the user
  to set up passwordless sudo, use root, or fall back to password auth).

- Cloud VPS (UpCloud) server creation: after hostname, ask whether to
  generate a password (as before) or supply a public SSH key, which gets
  added to the new server's root user (UpCloud skips password generation
  in that case).

Verified against a fake SSH server exercising all auth/sudo branches and
against the existing fake UpCloud harness (both auth paths through the
full creation wizard).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NFMuHFMb7r1xEwqxGw4pZn
